- op: discuss  # c699
  at: '2026-09-16T08:15:35Z'  # c699
  by: agent  # c699
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c699
  clock: 4  # c699
  nonce: c699  # c699
  message: "DONE 2026-09-16 by PR #999. Both halves of fix (c) shipped: (a) explicit mode\nno longer writes the manifest, (b) the pre-commit guard asserts the good mode.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE, as a differential rather than an assertion. Same command,\nsame tree, the pre-fix script restored from git and run from inside the repo:\n\n    ./scripts/<pre-fix smart-test> tests/test_catalogue_gate_terms.py\n        -> manifest replaced with \"# Mode: explicit\", 0 selected tests\n\n    ./scripts/smart-test tests/test_catalogue_gate_terms.py\n        -> manifest byte-identical, sha256 unchanged\n\nThe first attempt at that differential was CONTAMINATED and said so before I\nbelieved it: running the old script from the scratchpad made REPO_ROOT resolve\noutside the repo, so it never took the explicit path at all and wrote a\ntargeted manifest. Re-run from inside the tree, it reproduces exactly.\n\nFIX (a) is the load-bearing half, as this item said. An explicit run is not a\nselection computation -- it was never asked about the diff, and the honest\nthing for a command with no answer is to say nothing rather than publish an\nempty one. The run now states that it left the manifest untouched, because a\nsilent non-write is indistinguishable from a forgotten one.\n\nFIX (b) is the L54 correction this item named. .githooks/pre-commit rejected\nexactly `Mode: full-suite` and passed everything else through the else arm with\na GREEN tick. It now requires `Mode: targeted`, with a distinct reason per\nrejection so the message routes the reader to the right fix, and the test\nextracts the check and drives it against targeted / full-suite / explicit / an\nunrecognised mode -- the last being the point, since the whole defect was an\nenumerated blocklist.\n\nCORRECTION TO THIS ITEM'S \"THE EXISTING GATE DOES NOT CATCH IT\" ANALYSIS, which\nwas right about the hook and incomplete about CI. The live gate is Woodpecker,\nand .woodpecker/woodpecker.yml does not read `# Mode:` at all -- it reads\nSELECTED_TESTS and prints \"manifest selects no tests - skipping pytest\". So the\nexposure was not that CI mis-read the mode; it was that CI correctly read an\nEMPTY selection. (.github/workflows/ci.yml does enumerate full-suite the same\nblind way, but it is not the live gate, so it is recorded here rather than\nchanged.)\n\nTHE 2026-09-16 NARROWING STANDS AND IS NOT WHAT CLOSED THIS. auto-pr's\nregen+union repairs a wiped manifest before the PR exists, so the documented\nloop self-repaired; what stayed exposed was the manual-PR path,\nAUTO_PR_SKIP_MANIFEST=1, and the working tree between the wipe and the push.\nFix (a) removes the wipe itself, so none of those depend on a repair step now."  # c699
